+  Key design decisions:
+  - Synchronous handlers throughout (better-sqlite3 + scryptSync are sync) so Express 4 natively forwards thrown ApiErrors to the error middleware — no async-error pitfall.
+  - No external crypto dep — passwords hashed with Node's built-in scrypt (deps only include express/better-sqlite3/jsonwebtoken/uuid).
+  - Routers are auth-agnostic (read req.user only) so the unit tests' mock auth and the real JWT middleware both compose — auth is applied only in createApp, with POST /users and /users/login public.
+  - Tenant isolation enforced on every query; cross-tenant :id access returns 404.
+  - Funnel uses per-session greedy step-matching ordered by (timestamp, rowid), guaranteeing monotonic non-increasing counts even when batch events share a timestamp.
+  - Timeseries bucketed in JS (string-slicing) to avoid depending on the SQLite build's date-function behavior.
+
+  The review workflow is fanning out 5 dimension reviewers (spec compliance, tenant isolation, auth/security, query correctness, data edge-cases), then adversarially verifying each finding before I act on it. I'll report
